{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-retrofit-multiyear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.79: `userdb-retrofit-multiyear` -- THC and CO at running and start exhaust for the single-unit short-haul truck (52) and the combination long-haul truck (62), every fuel MOVES adds, in Washtenaw County, DEFAULT domain, 2015 AND 2020, August, weekday, hour 7, from the default database plus a USER INPUT DATABASE (`<databaseselections>`) holding thirteen On-Road Retrofit programs (`inputs/washtenaw-userdb-retrofit.esm`). A county domain database may hold one calendar year only, so a user database is how a retrofit table reaches a two-year run.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the calendar year. THC running on 62 is a phase-in -- rows at 2012 (model years 2000-2010, 20% retrofitted), 2015 (2005-2014, 40%), 2018 (2005-2012, 70%) and 2021 (2000-2020, 90%) -- and `rt_retrofitYear` picks, per calendar year and model year, the latest row at or before the year whose model years hold the cohort's: at 2015 the 2012 row for 2000-2004 (0.82) and the 2015 row for 2005-2014 (0.64); at 2020 the 2012 row for 2000-2004 still, the 2018 row for 2005-2012 (0.405) and the 2015 row for 2013-2014 (0.64). A later row replaces an earlier one only at the model years it names, and the 2021 row reaches neither year. CO on 52 at 2015 and 2020 reads the same 2015 rows (0.76, 0.66 where two overlap, 0.90), and start THC's 2020 row applies at 2020 alone. Execution database onRoadRetrofit: 8 of the 13 rows, InputDataManager's cut to THC and CO, running and start, diesel 52 and 62.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 3,552, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`: the years fold into the rate relation (conventions §98).\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "user-input-database",
      "multi-year",
      "control-strategy",
      "on-road-retrofit"
    ]
  },
